+# Feature Specification: Rental Module
+
+**Created**: 2026-10-21 | **Status**: Draft
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+
+### User Story 1 - Quote a rental (P1)
+Desk staff register equipment (board or sail, with a daily price) and ask what renting an item for a period costs.
+**Acceptance**:
+1. Given a board at 2500 cents/day, when quoting 2026-06-01T00:00:00Z to 2026-06-04T00:00:00Z (3 days), total is 7500.
+2. Given an unknown item, quoting fails.
+3. Given a period not on UTC midnights, empty or reversed, quoting fails.
+
+### User Story 2 - Book a rental (P1)
+Desk staff book an item for a period and receive a booking with an id and total.
+**Acceptance**:
+1. Given a free item, booking returns `{id, itemId, start, end, total}` matching the quote.
+2. Given an overlapping booking on the same item, booking fails and nothing is stored.
+3. Back-to-back periods (one ends where the next starts) do not overlap; other items are unaffected.
+
+### Edge Cases
+- Duplicate equipment id, invalid kind, non-integer/negative price: rejected.
+- Non-ISO or non-UTC strings (e.g. offset other than Z): rejected.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: Service is in-memory, created by `createRentalService()`.
+- **FR-002**: `addEquipment` accepts `{id, kind: 'board'|'sail', dailyPrice}`; dailyPrice is a non-negative integer of euro cents; duplicate ids rejected.
+- **FR-003**: Times are UTC ISO-8601; period start and end must be midnight UTC, start < end; end is exclusive.
+- **FR-004**: Total = number of days × dailyPrice, integer cents.
+- **FR-005**: `quote` throws for unknown item or invalid period.
+- **FR-006**: `book` throws for the same reasons, and when the item has an overlapping booking.
+- **FR-007**: Cancellation is out of scope; the 24h no-refund / otherwise full refund policy is recorded for later and not implemented.
+
+**Entities**: Equipment (id, kind, dailyPrice); Booking (id, itemId, start, end, total).
+
+## Success Criteria
+- SC-001: Every quote/booking total equals days × daily price exactly.
+- SC-002: No two bookings of one item ever overlap.
+
+## Assumptions
+- Returned start/end are the canonical ISO strings (`YYYY-MM-DDT00:00:00.000Z`).
+- Booking ids are unique strings.
